# Repo-wide ignores. Anything specific to one sub-project stays in that
# sub-project's own .gitignore — this file is only for things that land
# outside them, or in more than one of them.

# Next.js build output, wherever it lands.
#
# frontend/.gitignore already covers frontend/.next, and that is the copy you
# would expect. This rule is unanchored because `next dev` writes a second one
# outside the frontend directory entirely: Turbopack builds its Pages Router
# fallback bundle into <repo root>/<package.json "name">/.next/dev/static,
# which for this project means dhaka-route/. Nothing in next.config.ts asks for
# that and the documented turbopack.root detection does not explain it; it
# appears to be a Next 16 quirk in how the fallback project resolves its output
# directory.
.next/

# The directory that quirk creates. Anchored with a leading slash so it only
# matches at the repo root, and named separately from the rule above because it
# is a whole directory of nothing else — 7.7 MB of regenerated chunks, rebuilt
# on the next `npm run dev` and safe to delete at any time. Ignored rather than
# tolerated because `git add -A` would otherwise commit all of it.
/dhaka-route/
